EVALUATION OF THE PROPOSED FIX PLAN
1. OAuth Testing-mode 7-day refresh-token expiry is plausible only if OAuth consent is External + Testing; verify actual Cloud Console configuration. Re-authorize securely and update BLOGGER_OAUTH_JSON. Never share token JSON. Blogger email publishing is an optional route only if configured; it is not automatically more reliable.
2. A multi-provider chain is not implemented by listing provider names. Check current free-tier limits/terms, model access, credentials, and add adapter tests before switching.
3. A checked-in pre-recorded slogan is a strong low-cost fix; confirm rights/voice/pronunciation and test inclusion in every Reel.
4. Artifacts are scoped to workflow runs; use explicit run IDs/tokens or durable committed context.
5. Image prompt changes need end-to-end provider/cache/final-image QA.
6. Permalink verification is a hard acceptance criterion.

P0 WORK ORDER
1. Re-authorize Blogger OAuth securely and update the GitHub secret; publish one uniquely titled test article and capture post ID + canonical URL.
2. Make Blogger publication idempotent; verify title/body saved, published state, post ID/permalink; replace Google search scraping as primary verifier.
3. Fix the Reel slogan without Gemini dependency and repair reel-source-context contract; re-run row 23 through Telegram.
4. Fix Blogger brand identity Layout worker using DOM evidence, not arbitrary coordinates.
5. Audit image path end-to-end and hard-reject pharaonic visuals for modern legal topics.
6. Add provider fallbacks only after live quota/access checks and tests.
7. Run quality tests, then verify external outcomes.

ACCEPTANCE
- Blogger: new article has post ID + verified public permalink; retry does not duplicate; no false-positive success.
- Reel: row 23 branded playable MP4 + slogan audio + Telegram delivery confirmation.
- Images: no pharaonic imagery for current legal topics; QA inspects the exact uploaded file.
- Schedule: one deterministic variable slot per day, Cairo 10:00–22:00, no parity filter.
- Security: no secret values/session state in docs, logs, prompts, or repository.
